0..77 Comment "//! A hold at grade one. `var[1] c = e;` holds a value no one else holds: the"
78..156 Comment "//! value is made where the hold stands, and it is never copied while held. An"
157..237 Comment "//! exclusive access moves the value out to its view, the view is read once, and"
238..317 Comment "//! `resume` writes the new value back, so the write-back needs no count of the"
318..397 Comment "//! value\'s other holders. `var c = e;` holds at the default grade ω, and each"
398..463 Comment "//! read of it copies. The grades are those of graded modal types"
464..533 Comment "//! [Orchard-2019-quantitative_program_reasoning_graded_modal_types]."
534..537 Comment "//!"
538..615 Comment "//! - cites: [Orchard-2019-quantitative_program_reasoning_graded_modal_types]"
616..619 Comment "//!"
620..806 Comment "//! [Orchard-2019-quantitative_program_reasoning_graded_modal_types]: https://doi.org/10.1145/3341714 \"Orchard, Liepelt and Eades, Quantitative Program Reasoning with Graded Modal Types\""
